      "stream_token_id_count": 512,
      "text": "\n\nThis is a classic systems engineering trade-off. The choice between **Tensor Parallelism (TP)** and **Data Parallelism (DP)** (independent replicas) depends almost entirely on the size of the model relative to the GPU memory and the specific latency/throughput profile you need.\n\nHere is a detailed comparison across the dimensions you requested.\n\n### 1. Latency (Time to First Token & Inter-Token Latency)\n\n*   **Tensor Parallel (TP):**\n    *   **TTFT (Time to First Token):** Generally **lower**. The prompt is processed in parallel across all 4 GPUs. The computation is split, so the time to generate the first token is roughly $1/4$ of the time it would take on a single GPU (minus communication overhead).\n    *   **Inter-Token Latency (ITL):** **Lower**. During the autoregressive generation phase (generating token by token), the model weights are split. Each GPU computes a portion of the matrix multiplication. The result is a faster generation speed per token compared to a single GPU.\n    *   **Caveat:** There is a fixed overhead for All-Reduce communication at every layer. If the interconnect is slow, this overhead can eat into the gains.\n\n*   **Independent Replicas (DP):**\n    *   **TTFT:** **Higher**. Each request is handled by a single GPU. The entire prompt must be processed by one GPU's compute resources.\n    *   **ITL:** **Higher**. The generation speed is limited by the compute power of a single GPU.\n    *   **Caveat:** Latency is consistent per request, but you don't get the \"speedup\" from parallelizing the model itself.\n\n**Winner:** **Tensor Parallel** for low-latency, high-priority requests (e.g., interactive chat, real-time agents).\n\n### 2. Throughput (Tokens per Second / Requests per Second)\n\n*   **Tensor Parallel (TP):**\n    *   **Throughput:** **Lower** for high-concurrency workloads. TP is designed for *latency*, not *throughput*. You are using 4 GPUs to serve *one* request (or a small batch) faster. If you have 100 concurrent users, they are all competing for the same 4-GPU cluster.\n    *   **Batching:** You can still batch requests within the TP group, but the batch size is limited by",
