      "stream_token_id_count": 500,
      "text": "\n\n<think>\nThe user wants a technical guide for adding a new benchmark to an existing optimization repo. This is a practical, structured document. Let me think about what makes a good optimization benchmark repo structure and what the key concerns are:\n\n1. Where to put things (scripts, data, notes, patches, result summaries)\n2. Naming conventions for run directories\n3. Reproducibility requirements\n4. Validation criteria for promoting results\n\nLet me think about what a real optimization repo looks like. Think of repos like:\n- Compiler optimization benchmarks (LLVM, GCC)\n- Algorithm optimization repos\n- Performance tuning repos\n- Numerical optimization repos\n\nThe structure should be practical and opinionated. Let me write this as a clear, actionable guide with specific directory structures, naming conventions, and decision criteria. I'll make it feel like it's written by someone who has actually maintained such a repo and has opinions about what works.\n\nLet me structure this:\n- Directory layout\n- Naming conventions\n- What to record (reproducibility)\n- Validation/promotion criteria\n- A checklist or workflow\n\nI'll keep it technical, specific, and actionable. Not too long but thorough enough to be genuinely useful.\n</think>\n\n# Adding a New Benchmark to the Optimization Repo\n\n## 1. Directory Layout\n\nEvery benchmark lives under `benchmarks/<name>/`. Create the following skeleton before writing a single line of code:\n\n```\nbenchmarks/<name>/\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 README.md              # What, why, how to run, expected output\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 run.sh                 # Single entry point (bash or zsh)\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 src/                   # Benchmark source (the thing being optimized)\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 data/\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 inputs/            # Fixed input sets (committed, versioned)\n\u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 expected/          # Reference outputs / ground truth\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 patches/               # Candidate optimization patches (one per attempt)\n\u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 001-<slug>.patch\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 notes/\n\u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 <date>-<slug>.md  # Scratch analysis, hypotheses, dead ends\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 results/               # Run outputs (gitignored except summaries)\n\u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 <run-id>/\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 SUMMARY.md             # Promoted results table (committed)\n```\n\n**Rules of thumb:**\n\n- `data/inputs/` is committed. If a file",
